assistant: Subject: convert cent prices from vendor API 2026-10-01

Starting with `vendor-api-version: 2026-10-01`, the vendor sends `price` in cents (for example 119900 instead of 1199). `search_products` passed the value through unchanged, so prices came out 100× too high and broke the 20–2000 USD range rule. The handler now reads the `vendor-api-version` response header and divides `price` by 100 when the version is 2026-10-01 or later. Older responses are passed through as before, so the v1 fixtures give exactly the same output. Typecheck, lint and all 14 tests pass, including the repro test. I only changed `search_products`. `get_product` and the order tools read prices from the same vendor and may have the same problem on the new version, but I haven't checked them.

Subject: convert cent prices from vendor API 2026-10-01

